chromium.json is Docker's default seccomp profile with one change.

Source:  https://github.com/moby/moby/blob/docker-v29.2.1/vendor/github.com/moby/profiles/seccomp/default.json
Licence: Apache License 2.0, Copyright the Moby Project authors.

The change: the three rules that hold back user
namespaces — `clone` with the namespace flags masked off, the s390
variant of the same rule, and `clone3` answered with ENOSYS — are
replaced by one rule that permits `clone`, `clone3`, `setns` and
`unshare`. Chromium's renderer sandbox makes a user namespace, so the
default profile leaves the browser with no way in but `--no-sandbox`.
Playwright makes the same change in its own image; see
https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/main/utils/docker/seccomp_profile.json

To refresh the profile, take the file above from the Docker version
the daemon speaks to and apply the change again.
